{
    "series_title": "Before the Distance: The Story of John & Erin",
    "series_slug": "erin",
    "series_description": "An official five-song narrative story published by Ryan and Cassidy O'Connell of The Stardust Engine across Progress Street (2004) and Lost Sounds (2007). At Commonwealth Polytechnic Institute (CPI) in Blacksburg, Virginia, fraternal twins John and Erin navigate the steep Ironstone hills of campus in their power wheelchairs. When an accidental track skip from 'Seconds Into Forever' to 'Thunder in the Rain' at a Kincaid Hall speed-dating event places John across the table from a woman he doesn't realize will become his abuser, it takes Erin's split-second executive decision in the chaotic pre-Transit-Center curbside bus lineup along Commonwealth Mall beneath The Keystone Bridge ('Before the Distance') to pull her brother onto the Blue Ridge Transit bus before the steel doors close\u2014forging a sibling sanctuary ('Sanctuary in the Storm') that comes full circle when John protects Erin outside Kincaid Hall in 'Not Her'.",
